  "solution": {
    "text": "The constituents of nucleic acids are nitrogenous bases, sugar and phosphoric acid. The sugar present in DNA is D(-)-2-deoxyribose  and the sugar present in RNA is D(-) ribose. Due to these D(-)-sugar components, DNA and RNA molecules are chiral molecules.<br/><br/> <img src=\"assets\\st0004_71330b653f6e.jpeg\"/>"
  }
